---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Cloud & Multi-Tenancy Architecture" currentPath="/docs/guides/cloud-supabase-auth">
  <div class="space-y-8 font-sans text-xs">
    <div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-sky-400 font-semibold mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider">Cloud Roadmap</div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-sans">RouteNex Cloud & Team Multi-Tenancy</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm font-sans mt-1">Multi-tenant managed edge routing, workspace RBAC, and centralized billing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Dual-Edition Strategy</h2>
      <div class="space-y-2 text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        <div>• <strong class="text-white">RouteNex Open Source (Available Now):</strong> 100% self-hosted, offline, and zero-cloud authentication required. Launches locally with direct terminal setup tokens and local SQLite keystores.</div>
        <div>• <strong class="text-white">RouteNex Cloud (Coming Soon — Post-Beta):</strong> Fully managed edge proxy network, team workspace RBAC, multi-key pooling, audit logging, and team spend limits.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Join the Cloud Private Beta</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        RouteNex Cloud is currently in closed preview with select design partners. If your team needs managed edge gateways, central spend governance, or automated failover tunnels without hosting infrastructure, join the waitlist.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <a
          href="/pricing#waitlist"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-sky-500 hover:bg-sky-400 !text-zinc-950 font-semibold text-xs transition shadow-sm font-sans"
        >
          <span>Join Cloud Waitlist →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
